{"1862":{"n":1862,"cl":38,"id":"cma-163543","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Staff of Office","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"early to mid-1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2004.85"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The Yeke kingdom ruler Chief Msidi gave this as a gift of appreciation to the British missionary Frederick Stanley Arnot, whom the chief had invited to his kingdom.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","sculpture","wood-and-iron","african-art","central-africa","luba"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2004.85/2004.85_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1879":{"n":1879,"cl":38,"id":"cma-155499","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Memorial head (nsodie)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"late 1600s–early 1700s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1990.22"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The woman who sculpted this head did so without making a sketch, working from her memory of the subject.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["17th-century","sculpture","terracotta","african-art","ghana","akan-style-sculpture"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1990.22/1990.22_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1906":{"n":1906,"cl":38,"id":"cma-286706","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Ram Mask (Bolo)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"possibly early 1900s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2016.56"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The mask was vividly painted while in use. Look closely at its surface to see traces of blue, red, and white paint.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["20th-century","mask","african-art","africa","west-africa","wood-and-paint"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2016.56/2016.56_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1916":{"n":1916,"cl":38,"id":"cma-94940","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Lamellophone (chisanji)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"late 1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1915.495"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The CMA acquired this plucky instrument in 1915, one year before it opened to the public.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","musical-instrument","wood","iron","african-art","and-wire"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1915.495/1915.495_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1920":{"n":1920,"cl":38,"id":"cma-159880","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Prestige Cap (mpu ngola)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"late 1800s–early 1900s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1997.180"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The geometric motifs on this mpu cap—including diamonds and interlaces—are seen on Kongo, Vili, and Yombe works in other materials, including ivory and basketry.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","african-art","central-africa","africa","garment","republic-of-congo"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1997.180/1997.180_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1922":{"n":1922,"cl":38,"id":"cma-159000","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Head","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"thermoluminescence date 20–620 CE","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1995.21"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This complete head’s bold modeling, deliberate asymmetry, and sensitive expression make it one of the finest known examples of Nok sculpture.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["ancient","sculpture","terracotta","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.36},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1995.21/1995.21_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"1987":{"n":1987,"cl":38,"id":"cma-153765","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Commemorative figure (lefem)","creator":"Ateu Atsa","date":"mid-1800s–1910","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1987.62"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Ateu Atsa was both a famous and infamous artist! It is said that he enraged a ruler by portraying him realistically rather than in an idealized way, and was chased out of town after the sculpture was revealed.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","sculpture","wood","african-art","central-africa","africa"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.29},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1987.62/1987.62_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2534":{"n":2534,"cl":38,"id":"cma-149753","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Postscript from “Reverberations of Taiga”","creator":"Murata Kōkoku","date":"1910","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1979.73.2.36"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Kusakabe Meikaku, one of the three most famous Japanese calligraphers of his time, provided a title leaf, CMA 1979.73.1.1 , for a pair of albums of paintings after Ike Taiga (池大雅) (1723–1776) by his student Aoki Shukuya (青木夙夜) (died 1802).","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["20th-century","japan","ink-on-silk","japanese-art","portfolio","meiji-period-1868-1912"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.29},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.73.2.36/1979.73.2.36_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2555":{"n":2555,"cl":38,"id":"cma-144495","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Buffalo Mask","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"early to mid-1900s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1969.2"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Once broken, the right horn of this mask was repaired; this indicates that it was valued.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["20th-century","paint","wood","mask","plant-fibers","and-iron"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1969.2/1969.2_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2572":{"n":2572,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115163","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Disk Pendant (akrafokɔnmu)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1800s, before 1896","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.310"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Akan goldsmiths were organized into guilds, a kind of specialized group of artisans.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","jewelry","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.310/1935.310_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2585":{"n":2585,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115157","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Mask (Bwoom)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"mid- to late 1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.304"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Imagine this mask topped with eagle feathers; they would have been added only on special occasions when it was performed.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","mask","african-art","central-africa","africa","wood-and-paint"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.304/1935.304_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2590":{"n":2590,"cl":38,"id":"cma-136459","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Serpent Headdress","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"late 1800s–early 1900s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1960.37"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"In the context of boys' initiations, the serpent headdress was sometimes identified as the rainbow, which the Baga and their neighbors associate with beginnings and endings, life and death, and the continuation of lineages.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","mask","african-art","africa","west-africa","guinea"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1960.37/1960.37_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2612":{"n":2612,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115161","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Knife-sheath tip (sika boha)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.308"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Gold objects like this were frequently melted down to make new objects in new fashions.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","arms-and-armor","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.308/1935.308_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2630":{"n":2630,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115165","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Knife-sheath tip (sika boha)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.312"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Gold objects like this were frequently melted down to make new objects in new fashions.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","arms-and-armor","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.312/1935.312_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2644":{"n":2644,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115164","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Knife Handle Cover","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.311"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Only members of the goldsmiths' guild, who claimed descent from the first goldsmith Fusu Kwabi, could make gold ornaments for the royals and their entourage.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","arms-and-armor","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.311/1935.311_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2646":{"n":2646,"cl":38,"id":"cma-129836","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Pendant: Crocodile","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1930 or earlier","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1952.265"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"A goldsmith had to create superfine rolls of wax to make the texture of this piece; the wax was used to make a mold into which liquid gold was poured.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","jewelry","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1952.265/1952.265_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2670":{"n":2670,"cl":38,"id":"cma-115162","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Knife-sheath tip (sika boha)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1800s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.309"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This chape would have been secured to the very tip of a knife sheath, modeled after European style sheaths.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","gold","arms-and-armor","african-art","africa","west-africa"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.25},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.309/1935.309_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2686":{"n":2686,"cl":38,"id":"cma-166209","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Female Mask (Gambanda or Kambanda)","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"early 1900s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2008.150"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This female mask would have performed in a collective multimedia event with audience participation.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["20th-century","wood","mask","african-art","plant-fiber","and-colorant"],"ton